    "advancement": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>If you choose the Grimoire of Sacrifice, you instead can use the Demonic Core of the Succubus. The demonic core of a succubus resembles...a tube of lipstick? A warlock who carries the demonic core of a succubus gains the following benefits:</p><p><strong>2nd Level:</strong> While carrying a succubus's core, the warlock has advantage on Charisma (Deception) and Charisma (Persuasion) checks. While they hold the core, they can cast the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.eS7XnnApoxRxYXPs]{charm person} spell at will.</p><p><strong>5th Level:</strong> While holding the core, the warlock knows the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.zMAWdyc8UVb37BK4]{suggestion} spell and can cast it without expending a warlock spell slot once per long rest.</p><p><strong>9th Level:</strong> While holding the core, the warlock knows the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.91Sw6vOIaO7U8DvM]{dominate person} spell and can cast it without expending a warlock spell slot once per long rest.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
